# Required tools

**Normative registry** for tools this center expects on the operator machine.
Missions that install or verify tooling **must** read this file — do not invent
a second required-tools list.

When adding a tool later, append a row under **Tool inventory** with every
required field. Prefer official docs and install pages; keep dry-run commands
executable without further browsing.

## Schema (per tool)

| Field | Required | Meaning |
|-------|----------|---------|
| **`id`** | yes | Stable kebab-case tool id (also usual CLI name when identical) |
| **`cli`** | yes | Primary command name for PATH probes when the install path is absent |
| **`minVersion`** | yes | Minimum semver (or tool-native version string) the center accepts |
| **`docsUrl`** | yes | Primary documentation URL |
| **`installUrl`** | yes | Installation documentation URL (may equal docs when install is a subsection) |
| **`macosInstallPath`** | yes | Canonical path of the binary after the sole macOS method succeeds (tilde allowed) |
| **`windowsInstallPath`** | yes | Canonical path of the binary after the sole Windows method succeeds (`%VAR%` allowed) |
| **`macosMethods`** | yes | Ordered list of install method ids allowed on macOS — **exactly one** sole method |
| **`windowsMethods`** | yes | Ordered list of install method ids allowed on Windows — **exactly one** sole method |
| **`dryRuns`** | yes | Ordered list of `{ command, expect }` checks after install |

**Install paths** are the **authoritative** location for probe and invoke after a
registry install (and the first probe target when checking for an existing
install). Expand `~` and Windows `%VAR%` in the agent shell. Agents **must**
invoke the tool via the resolved install path when that file exists; use bare
**`cli`** on PATH only when the install path is missing and a PATH hit is found
(for example a pre-registry install the user kept via **`use-path`**).

**Method ids** label the sole install procedure for that OS. Procedure detail lives
on **`installUrl`** and in the method notes. Agents **must not** invent methods
absent from the tool’s `macosMethods` / `windowsMethods` lists. When a list has
one entry, that id is **mandatory** — **do not** ask the user to pick a method
or an install directory (paths are fixed by **`macosInstallPath`** /
**`windowsInstallPath`**).

## Tool inventory

### `rclone`

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **id** | `rclone` |
| **cli** | `rclone` |
| **minVersion** | `1.60.0` |
| **docsUrl** | https://rclone.org/docs/ |
| **installUrl** | https://rclone.org/install/ |
| **macosInstallPath** | `~/bin/rclone` |
| **windowsInstallPath** | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\rclone\rclone.exe` |

**macOS methods (`macosMethods`):**

| Method id | Notes (from install docs — follow `installUrl` for exact commands) |
|-----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `curl` | **Sole** macOS method. Download the official **precompiled** macOS binary from downloads.rclone.org (see `installUrl`) via **curl** — do **not** run `install.sh`. Create the parent of **`macosInstallPath`** if missing; install the binary at **`macosInstallPath`**; `chmod +x`. Ensure the parent directory is on PATH when dry-runs use bare **`cli`**. **Forbidden:** `sudo`; system paths (`/usr/local/bin`, etc.); brew; MacPorts; `install.sh`; other install locations. |

**Windows methods (`windowsMethods`):**

| Method id | Notes (from install docs — follow `installUrl` for exact commands) |
|-----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `fixed-path-exe` | **Sole** Windows method. Download the official Windows zip from downloads.rclone.org (see `installUrl`). Extract **`rclone.exe`** to **`windowsInstallPath`** (create directories as needed). Ensure that directory is on the user PATH when dry-runs use bare **`cli`**. **Forbidden:** asking the user for a different install folder; offering winget or an open-ended extract location. |

**dryRuns:**

| # | `command` | `expect` |
|---|-----------|----------|
| 1 | `rclone version` | Exit **0**; stdout includes a version ≥ **`minVersion`** |
| 2 | `rclone listremotes` | Exit **0** (empty remote list is OK) |

Prefer running **`dryRuns`** with the resolved **`macosInstallPath`** /
**`windowsInstallPath`** as the executable (substitute the path for the leading
**`cli`** token). Bare **`cli`** is allowed only when invoking via PATH after a
confirmed PATH hit.

## Agent obligations

1. Treat this inventory as the **only** required-tools source for this center.
2. Probe in order: (a) resolved **`macosInstallPath`** / **`windowsInstallPath`**
   for the current OS; (b) any **user-supplied path/command** from the install
   mission gate; (c) `command -v` / PATH on **`cli`**. Do not invent alternate
   install directories.
3. Compare discovered version to **`minVersion`** — classify **ok**, **outdated**,
   or **missing**.
4. Install only after structured-choice consent to **install** (not method/path
   choice). Use the **sole** listed OS method id; place the binary exactly at
   **`macosInstallPath`** / **`windowsInstallPath`**; follow method notes and
   **`installUrl`**. **Forbidden:** method pickers; install-directory questions.
5. After install (or path override), run **every** **`dryRuns`** row in order
   (prefer install-path executable) and record pass/fail.

